rrier identity, canonical hash binding, and transmitted-material readback are outside this mathematical judgment, and I make no runtime-attestation claim.\\\",\\\"checks\\\":{\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"H001-H004 are the direct inputs, and the prose's main claims about the characteristic, weight range, divided powers, and lattice refer to those stated inputs. No external premise is cited.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0\\\",\\\"/inputs/1\\\",\\\"/inputs/2\\\",\\\"/inputs/3\\\",\\\"/inference/inputs\\\"]},\\\"argument\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"S001-S004 give a plausible route through divided-power calculations, matrix units, the rank-one lattice, and reduction. At S005, however, writing w=sum_i c_i e_i and concluding e_j in W requires the e_i to be the basis vectors of the K-module. The earlier declaration defines e_i in V(lambda) over C; S004's reduced basis consists of images of a e_i, not those vectors as such. This is the first unsupported step in the supplied prose. No alternative proof is supplied here.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\"]},\\\"dependency_accounting\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"S005's basis expansion and matrix-unit application depend on the identification of the reduced basis with the e_i used there. S004 states a scalar-extension identification, and the local b_i declaration names images, but S005 does not invoke or consistently use those objects. The missing connection is needed for the decisive implication, so the factual-use accounting is incomplete at that point.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\"]},\\\"output\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"UNVERIFIED\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The conclusion states nonzeroness and the invariant-subspace criterion, and S005 purports to establish both. Since its basis argument is not closed as written, the exact output is not established.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"W is introduced as an arbitrary invariant K-subspace at S005 and the reasoning is intended to prove it is zero or the whole module; no temporary assumption or witness is exported. The defect identified is the basis-object mismatch, not an assumption-discharge error.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/12\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/13\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"applicability\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"There are no E/M source inputs or source applications. H inputs are used directly; no external-theorem applicability mapping is implicated.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inference/applications\\\"]},\\\"statement_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The packet states the target's nonzero and invariant-subspace meaning, and each H input is fully written in the packet. No theorem name or inherited equation number is needed to understand the conclusion. This judgment does not cure the proof defect.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/1/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/2/statement\\\",\\\"/inputs/3/statement\\\",\\\"/output/statement\\\"]},\\\"object_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The actual use of e_i in S005 treats it as a vector in M tensor_Z K, but its declaration is as y^i v/i! in the complex V(lambda). The local b_i declaration separately names the images in the reduced/scalar-extended module, and S004 refers to the basis a e_i. S005's actual occurrences do not identify e_i with those images. Therefore the actual mathematical objects in the decisive calculation are not consistently declared in that domain.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"dependency_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The conclusion that all basis vectors lie in W uses a basis of the K-module, but the stated calculation uses e_i without establishing that these are the reduced/scalar-extended basis vectors. The local declaration b_i and the basis discussion in S004 do not repair the actual unlinked use in S005 under packet-only review.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\"]},\\\"packet_replay\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"On the packet alone, the proof is insufficient as written at S005 for the basis-object reason above. This is the present packet-only review; no source or other inference proof was used. The mathematical judgment does not authenticate carrier identity, canonical hash binding, or transmitted-material readback.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/14\\\"]}}}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explici